From 8cdfcc8e0feb3689a1ec1d292539af083b13ea94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naster17 <naster17.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:46:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Enable native gfx1013 Torch hipSPARSELt integration

The old build cache predates the installed hipSPARSELt package, and the Torch
architecture gate excluded gfx1013. Enable the native scalar path, validate its
pack/layout/epilogue contracts, and expose HIP version/search bindings. Report
availability from compiled support rather than every ROCm build. Initialize
search fields before returning them.

Test Plan:
```text
python -m pip install -e . -v --no-build-isolation
python test_bc250_hipsparselt.py -v
spin lint -- test/test_bc250_hipsparselt.py aten/src/ATen/native/sparse/cuda/cuSPARSELtOps.cpp torch/CMakeLists.txt torch/csrc/Module.cpp torch/csrc/cuda/Module.cpp torch/csrc/cuda/shared/cusparselt.cpp
lintrunner -a
```
Separate candidate on BC-250: 20 GPU tests passed, 120 small CPU-reference
matmuls, pack decoding, public wrappers/search and 14 refusals. Guard ACK and
kernel log unchanged. Lint attempts could not initialize the missing offline
lint environment; no lint success claimed. Original Torch remains preserved.
No sparse speedup or broad stability claim.

Authored with an AI assistant.
